values ('f2a3b4c5-6d7e-4f64-9c34-4d5e6f7a8b04', 'sculpture', 'Sculpture', 'This course introduces sculpture as a material, spatial, conceptual, and social practice. Students learn foundational 3-D design, additive and subtractive processes, construction, casting, assemblage, installation, site-specific practice, digital fabrication, critique, documentation, and professional exhibition methods. The course balances technical skill, material intelligence, historical literacy, contemporary theory, and ambitious studio production.');

