  'Sculpture',
  'Sculpture',
  'This course introduces sculpture as a material, spatial, conceptual, and social practice. Students learn foundational 3-D design, additive and subtractive processes, construction, casting, assemblage, installation, site-specific practice, digital fabrication, critique, documentation, and professional exhibition methods. The course balances technical skill, material intelligence, historical literacy, contemporary theory, and ambitious studio production.',
  $sculjson${"slug": "sculpture", "title": "Sculpture", "description": "This course introduces sculpture as a material, spatial, conceptual, and social practice. Students learn foundational 3-D design, additive and subtractive processes, construction, casting, assemblage, installation, site-specific practice, digital fabrication, critique, documentation, and professional exhibition methods. The course balances technical skill, material intelligence, historical literacy, contemporary theory, and ambitious studio production.", "topics": [{"id": "f05c29af-eded-4876-95bb-08c74437841d", "type": "topic", "title": "Sculpture as Object, Space, Material, and Experience", "description": "This opening unit frames sculpture as more than an object. Students learn to think across material presence, spatial placement, viewer movement, historical reference, and lived experience.", "children": [{"id": "92464d2a-7215-433d-a6b7-72b3b35e63fc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Object and Thingness", "children": [{"id": "2e1ba199-c89f-4f8d-808e-bf33f55d968a", "type": "concept", "title": "Objecthood and material presence"}, {"id": "09c10986-2954-4309-a293-192aa5cc192a", "type": "concept", "title": "Autonomy versus context"}, {"id": "3763837c-1cb8-4f70-ab9c-6244581d389f", "type": "concept", "title": "Pedestals, supports, and display conventions"}, {"id": "6998a1e8-cce4-4e5f-8704-ca61d12c3a4f", "type": "concept", "title": "Touch, proximity, and bodily scale"}], "description": "Students learn why sculptural meaning begins with physical presence: weight, surface, size, resistance, orientation, and how an object occupies attention."}, {"id": "7166ef05-f741-4697-bf1a-3701c8b32f0f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Space and Viewer Experience", "children": [{"id": "fffa32ee-df14-4769-8628-fe3c9eb17916", "type": "concept", "title": "Frontality and all-around viewing"}, {"id": "6d061c77-20be-4b29-8d2e-6d73cd2dab25", "type": "concept", "title": "Sight lines and circulation"}, {"id": "e85ca964-086d-44d5-9780-f08f1380d9d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Void, interval, and negative space"}, {"id": "056295ad-d647-4352-90f3-3ce8f737571e", "type": "concept", "title": "Temporal experience and sequence"}], "description": "The point is to see sculpture as something encountered through movement rather than absorbed from a single fixed viewpoint."}, {"id": "0135cc58-930d-432f-bd22-e51154732fe1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Concept, Context, and Encounter", "children": [{"id": "6b36cf25-04ff-48ef-bb73-52243def2c1e", "type": "concept", "title": "Site and institutional context"}, {"id": "48441443-b54f-48c1-bc01-45586be456be", "type": "concept", "title": "Narrative, symbol, and metaphor"}, {"id": "d3205542-1517-4a12-859e-7ffd500fd908", "type": "concept", "title": "Embodiment and phenomenology"}, {"id": "0008ea9a-94c8-4033-9cca-792aa8ba64ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Audience, participation, and interpretation"}], "description": "Students connect formal choices to ideas, locations, histories, and audiences so that making decisions carry intellectual force."}]}, {"id": "8b031c1a-5d88-4900-b144-f6961b55f203", "type": "topic", "title": "Three-Dimensional Design: Form, Volume, Mass, Scale, and Space", "description": "This unit builds the visual grammar of 3-D work. Students learn to compose with form, mass, volume, scale, proportion, gravity, and spatial relationships before committing to complex materials.", "children": [{"id": "0bd1d0fe-2242-40cd-830b-5101da26bfa7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Form, Volume, and Mass", "children": [{"id": "5ed7dc4b-4ced-4304-b305-3bbfa27d145c", "type": "concept", "title": "Geometric and organic form"}, {"id": "73e0bb8e-8356-4cfa-8582-7e03292cba45", "type": "concept", "title": "Solid mass versus implied volume"}, {"id": "b6453db6-3217-42c6-b5cd-9493668de070", "type": "concept", "title": "Positive and negative space"}, {"id": "bba820f9-d6d6-4674-a50c-97ec8e3eeae7", "type": "concept", "title": "Proportion, rhythm, and repetition"}], "description": "Students develop control over the basic sculptural elements that make an object feel light, dense, dynamic, stable, compressed, or expansive."}, {"id": "55424d1c-3b2b-4984-af10-2526d485dd06", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scale and Human Reference", "children": [{"id": "e6c4371d-9bfd-42c4-9632-9e4e1907765f", "type": "concept", "title": "Maquettes and scale models"}, {"id": "b1725d14-4f4e-4e4e-8dcb-7a8d9f2825e1", "type": "concept", "title": "Body scale and ergonomic reference"}, {"id": "6f8df4b2-7cf4-4eb3-ba4d-b28cdbe6e99d", "type": "concept", "title": "Monumentality and intimacy"}, {"id": "d0a5dda0-30fc-49f0-ae68-a4fb6dfacecd", "type": "concept", "title": "Measurement, enlargement, and translation"}], "description": "The gist is learning how scale changes meaning, from hand-held object to architectural intervention to public monument."}, {"id": "baec9511-d1b8-4be3-b769-95f5ea651ccb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Balance, Gravity, and Spatial Tension", "children": [{"id": "f157a4f8-b8f3-4b17-84b3-865d22cbf919", "type": "concept", "title": "Center of gravity"}, {"id": "74652923-57b8-48f5-92de-825ff70cb328", "type": "concept", "title": "Cantilever and counterweight"}, {"id": "c604b5cb-ac18-4c41-bf13-41e7ba79bb05", "type": "concept", "title": "Symmetry and asymmetry"}, {"id": "a5d996a7-22ea-4cef-bbdf-e1bcdda8fadc", "type": "concept", "title": "Visual tension versus physical stability"}], "description": "Students learn that sculpture must persuade both the eye and the body; it has to look intentional and often has to stand safely."}]}, {"id": "64988136-2eae-43a7-88c6-733d11754df4", "type": "topic", "title": "Materials, Tools, Studio Safety, and Shop Literacy", "description": "A world-class sculpture course treats safety and shop literacy as creative infrastructure. Students learn to choose materials intelligently, handle tools responsibly, and plan work before risks accumulate.", "children": [{"id": "be755742-0fb4-4f7d-be5c-7c6dd0f3017f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Material Families and Properties", "children": [{"id": "518703fb-92ab-4911-a15c-e6c790b665ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Clay, plaster, wood, metal, foam, plastics, textiles"}, {"id": "d6784ac9-caf0-4083-b67a-a7cfec67c31d", "type": "concept", "title": "Structural and surface properties"}, {"id": "1fe7636a-48e2-45f4-8503-9ab0da6ac347", "type": "concept", "title": "Archival and temporary materials"}, {"id": "e9f7dad8-8f53-4ca9-aec2-9cc300eb876a", "type": "concept", "title": "Material tests and sample boards"}], "description": "Students compare materials by strength, flexibility, weight, toxicity, workability, cost, durability, and expressive potential."}, {"id": "197ad5c7-9084-4f85-9c6a-3e3e3dad7aae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Tool Use and Shop Workflow", "children": [{"id": "9ad2c71f-017a-49c3-8474-bac36087afae", "type": "concept", "title": "Hand tools and power tools"}, {"id": "5e1a2cf2-1169-4057-a235-316077e9d694", "type": "concept", "title": "Clamps, vises, jigs, and fixtures"}, {"id": "7ae9d1e8-daf8-4582-8314-7cb5c2e9a778", "type": "concept", "title": "Measuring, marking, cutting, and assembly"}, {"id": "8079811b-ce93-4b2a-82cf-00d03b656b1e", "type": "concept", "title": "Maintenance, storage, and cleanup routines"}], "description": "The point is to make students more independent in the studio while respecting shared equipment and time."}, {"id": "a46ad3c8-440b-47b8-91af-8dd1c2117f2d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Safety, Risk, and Documentation", "children": [{"id": "a73ff11f-4fde-42b3-9cd0-3fd9c7441c00", "type": "concept", "title": "Personal protective equipment"}, {"id": "b891efcd-38ff-4164-91b7-98e81dedcb75", "type": "concept", "title": "Ventilation, dust, solvents, and fumes"}, {"id": "d4e66dca-9898-4c64-a04e-113ecc1de892", "type": "concept", "title": "Material safety data sheets"}, {"id": "9bab3649-b5d3-4752-b419-1525b2e60037", "type": "concept", "title": "Lifting, transport, and emergency procedures"}], "description": "Students learn to make risk visible before they cut, cast, weld, sand, spray, lift, or install."}]}, {"id": "08dc9974-d480-4f74-9534-b287798010a2", "type": "topic", "title": "Additive Modeling: Clay, Wax, Plaster, Armatures, and Figure Construction", "description": "Additive modeling develops the hand, eye, and ability to build form gradually. Students work from gesture and mass toward structure, anatomy, surface, and expressive refinement.", "children": [{"id": "64eebbb4-71eb-4608-99da-9fc12d08de66", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Clay, Wax, and Plaster Modeling", "children": [{"id": "aa2a6400-ba54-47e2-9ced-d214d85d935d", "type": "concept", "title": "Coils, slabs, modeling, and joining"}, {"id": "0063d9f4-40eb-4634-a144-fff073813b8d", "type": "concept", "title": "Wax modeling and repair"}, {"id": "05b5c02a-202c-4162-ab53-ca34649306b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Plaster buildup and carving back"}, {"id": "d5e6b2fc-6f79-47c1-a9e1-4f31cba72e0a", "type": "concept", "title": "Drying, curing, and cracking control"}], "description": "Students learn materials that invite revision, compression, addition, and expressive touch."}, {"id": "0a28038a-6a08-4fd6-8e67-e90432d94da1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Armatures and Internal Support", "children": [{"id": "66fe3f13-ec07-4a9a-9fb7-4c19eb5d0d3b", "type": "concept", "title": "Wire, pipe, wood, and mixed armatures"}, {"id": "82e60471-d95d-4c5f-b7c7-3f4861e876aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Load, balance, and anchor points"}, {"id": "e5212dd5-6894-4d8f-b35b-391a4231e5aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Removable versus embedded supports"}, {"id": "7501dd60-9bb6-4c42-909b-5b261cb10b2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Compatibility with clay, plaster, and casting"}], "description": "The gist is learning that hidden structure shapes what the surface can do."}, {"id": "b1dd393f-84e6-4e68-aecd-01373fda5125", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Figure, Gesture, and Surface", "children": [{"id": "48909b4f-91d0-42d7-a9bc-30be7737ee87", "type": "concept", "title": "Gesture and pose"}, {"id": "5193f3b6-d749-4207-bc6a-fd3542659c7d", "type": "concept", "title": "Proportion and skeletal landmarks"}, {"id": "58e5f797-1b7a-4f4f-8342-2a7591d55677", "type": "concept", "title": "Plane changes and anatomy overview"}, {"id": "951f83d3-159e-408f-88a6-790472026314", "type": "concept", "title": "Texture, tool marks, and finish"}], "description": "Students learn how body-based observation strengthens both representational and abstract sculpture."}]}, {"id": "7584b66a-2a78-49d3-95dd-fe523edd9618", "type": "topic", "title": "Subtractive Processes: Carving, Cutting, Shaping, and Surface", "description": "Subtractive methods teach commitment, patience, and the intelligence of removal. Students learn how form emerges through cutting, carving, sanding, scraping, and surface decisions.", "children": [{"id": "b2181331-c9d0-437e-82f6-f4c23ebbfc6f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Carving Logic", "children": [{"id": "58dcdc81-466e-4c11-968e-abfd28bd1116", "type": "concept", "title": "Block planning and profile drawings"}, {"id": "30656c5f-7f64-477d-91d2-9ac11a8c69eb", "type": "concept", "title": "Roughing, refining, and finishing"}, {"id": "99ac64ae-e9a7-42f3-a9c5-40fc880531d9", "type": "concept", "title": "Grain, direction, and fracture"}, {"id": "8015d103-e6f9-4705-a2d4-66a8de37f432", "type": "concept", "title": "Relief versus freestanding carving"}], "description": "Students learn to think from the outside inward, preserving what matters while removing what does not."}, {"id": "4971a7e1-c691-4c30-a934-03a9b007358e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Materials for Subtractive Work", "children": [{"id": "a9e166dd-c16c-4059-9a40-a7ca5f747e59", "type": "concept", "title": "Foam and plaster blocks"}, {"id": "bcb56d8e-6c5f-4cd2-b9d1-7aec536a58b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Wood species and grain behavior"}, {"id": "931a67b2-f603-40d5-9385-4f4da6845c83", "type": "concept", "title": "Stone overview and tool limits"}, {"id": "9da83b98-e931-44a7-aa7b-4b10acf31db3", "type": "concept", "title": "Composite and reclaimed materials"}], "description": "The point is to match tool, material, and ambition so the process is feasible and expressive."}, {"id": "24e55257-9857-423c-85b5-1f295f978772", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Surface and Edge Control", "children": [{"id": "330d32ee-21c5-4e8a-aad8-00aa6959203d", "type": "concept", "title": "Rasps, files, chisels, knives, and sandpaper"}, {"id": "bb80d6d6-e7d0-4c1c-b936-2d6c6588d3b9", "type": "concept", "title": "Edge sharpness and softness"}, {"id": "604a8bd2-e923-4ee1-b1ef-f53672e9160b", "type": "concept", "title": "Texture as evidence of process"}, {"id": "332bc089-b60d-4335-8e92-eaca3e1ba938", "type": "concept", "title": "Sealing, polishing, painting, and repair"}], "description": "Students learn that carving is not finished when the shape appears; surface is part of the idea."}]}, {"id": "ae6cff81-77ce-4dd4-85ce-6b0ee38199ca", "type": "topic", "title": "Construction: Wood, Metal, Fasteners, Welding, Joinery, and Structural Logic", "description": "Construction joins separate parts into a sculptural whole. Students learn structural thinking, fabrication sequencing, material compatibility, and the difference between a joint that merely holds and one that contributes meaning.", "children": [{"id": "5cfd8224-f777-4ce3-9f64-13d6c25ac8ae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Wood and Joinery", "children": [{"id": "63f97fcc-c83c-4ceb-91ee-42f38c913614", "type": "concept", "title": "Measuring, cutting, drilling, and sanding"}, {"id": "8fbf6975-52ce-4d9f-9faf-d40134911adc", "type": "concept", "title": "Butt, lap, miter, and dowel joints"}, {"id": "9b7da7a2-8fbc-4f45-bcee-2ec1bd1a947a", "type": "concept", "title": "Screws, bolts, glue, and clamps"}, {"id": "fefd2402-1aef-4afd-875a-3233ebf12664", "type": "concept", "title": "Frames, boxes, bases, and armatures"}], "description": "Students learn basic woodworking as a foundation for frames, supports, pedestals, and finished sculptural forms."}, {"id": "e1141d64-ef73-4b69-9a2b-528e41d78e7f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Metal and Welding Overview", "children": [{"id": "a9590fe3-88fb-4572-988c-01732a75a71b", "type": "concept", "title": "Cutting, grinding, drilling, and bending"}, {"id": "f34a2d16-893a-4e92-9485-14b52417d58e", "type": "concept", "title": "Welding concepts and shop protocols"}, {"id": "4a0d3990-f799-4b12-842d-08dd748b7e20", "type": "concept", "title": "Fasteners and mechanical connections"}, {"id": "a5b3797c-daba-4364-a0ff-db9e160389be", "type": "concept", "title": "Rust, patina, paint, and finish"}], "description": "The gist is to understand metal as line, mass, structure, and surface, with strong attention to supervised safety."}, {"id": "853d1868-1d0c-4a3c-89b2-4306a057ae5f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Structural Logic and Fabrication Plans", "children": [{"id": "25b56cb7-3c45-4829-9c6b-1b1aa70e8c93", "type": "concept", "title": "Load paths and stress points"}, {"id": "ca89c8af-4e79-4d2b-8ac2-8ae642427886", "type": "concept", "title": "Modular construction and disassembly"}, {"id": "fdd0adcf-9005-4b2d-b2c1-d6dd6df2f90c", "type": "concept", "title": "Templates, jigs, and mockups"}, {"id": "8dfdf7a5-1061-42f0-a818-2bd3d8ec9aad", "type": "concept", "title": "Transport, storage, and installation constraints"}], "description": "Students learn to design the making process before the final object fails or becomes impossible to transport."}]}, {"id": "b51c5ebb-0327-4af3-ba2d-3887ec834b9b", "type": "topic", "title": "Casting and Moldmaking: Plaster, Resin, Rubber, Bronze Overview, and Multiples", "description": "Casting and moldmaking introduce replication, translation, and transformation. Students learn how a form can move across materials, scales, editions, and levels of finish.", "children": [{"id": "deda63f9-e31e-4f43-bbec-583ed0b216b3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mold Types and Planning", "children": [{"id": "27df011f-cdc1-4a89-bba6-6ff78df1ca40", "type": "concept", "title": "One-part and two-part molds"}, {"id": "8f89713d-3e9d-4fa0-bdb3-cf91e59193e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Flexible rubber molds"}, {"id": "41797108-3073-441c-8642-9688e491eb2a", "type": "concept", "title": "Keys, registration, and release agents"}, {"id": "43d1047e-3386-4dc6-bce4-63d170bc0bd1", "type": "concept", "title": "Undercuts, vents, and pour gates"}], "description": "Students learn that mold design is sculptural problem-solving: every undercut, seam, key, and pour path matters."}, {"id": "a003b408-da4a-40f7-8866-d861ead4a85e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Casting Materials and Processes", "children": [{"id": "11da7daa-aa4b-41ca-9d29-45f547a55c81", "type": "concept", "title": "Plaster, cement, wax, resin, and slip overview"}, {"id": "824f8c33-81cc-49bf-893b-38e5a23b796b", "type": "concept", "title": "Mixing ratios and cure times"}, {"id": "5af3c223-080a-48fd-8f69-fa5e45a6fea3", "type": "concept", "title": "Colorants, fillers, and inclusions"}, {"id": "78ada06a-3625-4ec8-af34-cf2eede4761b", "type": "concept", "title": "Defects, bubbles, repairs, and cleanup"}], "description": "The point is to understand how different casting materials behave and what each adds to meaning."}, {"id": "b76809d7-aa60-4169-b671-0e4e196b0fe3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Editions, Multiples, and Bronze Overview", "children": [{"id": "1cdda518-d77e-4883-89a9-3f3b19e1442d", "type": "concept", "title": "Editioning and record keeping"}, {"id": "7ee0f313-0796-466b-9780-0d4637c0780e", "type": "concept", "title": "Lost-wax bronze concepts"}, {"id": "3bde1525-ed2c-4ab3-9c62-a1ab387f407a", "type": "concept", "title": "Foundry collaboration and safety"}, {"id": "fcf6f890-d1a4-4ce6-acd2-67b046e4283a", "type": "concept", "title": "Multiples, series, and installation strategies"}], "description": "Students learn casting as a way to think about repetition, variation, value, and professional production."}]}, {"id": "c1707b26-f30e-43fc-bb0e-307354939c46", "type": "topic", "title": "Assemblage, Found Objects, Mixed Media, and Readymade Strategies", "description": "Assemblage and found-object work sharpen selection, context, and juxtaposition. Students learn how existing materials carry histories and how composition can redirect those histories.", "children": [{"id": "03a46747-9636-4c26-b19a-d58bb7ca3829", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Readymade and Object Selection", "children": [{"id": "4de8f4b5-ff37-4564-94c7-1de20433c8df", "type": "concept", "title": "Duchamp and readymade traditions"}, {"id": "2fa6664f-125a-44ca-8c67-162959752171", "type": "concept", "title": "Commodity, tool, archive, and relic"}, {"id": "467a1b0c-3955-44ab-b7df-f6809767687c", "type": "concept", "title": "Humor, irony, and displacement"}, {"id": "91d401da-78a7-4312-b44a-8a5639270bfa", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethics of source, ownership, and representation"}], "description": "Students learn to see ordinary objects as carriers of use, class, labor, memory, design, and cultural meaning."}, {"id": "c9083c94-44f1-4844-a074-1aa957e5f0a5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Assemblage and Mixed Media", "children": [{"id": "ee2a8f23-4b6f-4b3b-92b5-e089cd9cbc46", "type": "concept", "title": "Accumulation and collage in space"}, {"id": "45476d9e-feae-4d7a-aae0-a6eb1913b9cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Fastening incompatible materials"}, {"id": "ffeddf98-614b-4175-84fc-8b2354403fb0", "type": "concept", "title": "Text, image, sound, light, and video elements"}, {"id": "5953f0c8-e3b7-4d10-a3e8-2552c37b2298", "type": "concept", "title": "Surface transitions and visual hierarchy"}], "description": "The gist is learning how unlike materials can hold together formally, structurally, and conceptually."}, {"id": "5fcc304d-a98c-4f9a-8c8d-deaf50cd18ab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Material Culture and Meaning", "children": [{"id": "a2563bbc-d816-45e1-9e91-4880ee0cf66e", "type": "concept", "title": "Domestic, industrial, and public objects"}, {"id": "d8dc4f54-d713-4c51-8283-99270a4ec4ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Memory, trauma, identity, and place"}, {"id": "0e873718-0836-475c-8c09-9ecdbc03c7af", "type": "concept", "title": "Waste, reuse, and environmental critique"}, {"id": "3aaea0e0-295e-4767-950d-242389d4c2d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Display as argument"}], "description": "Students learn to read objects socially, historically, politically, and personally."}]}, {"id": "1899a9ec-e1e5-4084-b3c9-049848771d7e", "type": "topic", "title": "Installation, Site-Specific, Public, and Socially Engaged Sculpture", "description": "This unit moves sculpture beyond the isolated studio object. Students learn to design for rooms, sites, institutions, publics, landscapes, communities, and viewer participation.", "children": [{"id": "4733812f-f458-4ec9-b169-c3441cf5a0fd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Installation and Spatial Sequence", "children": [{"id": "8c2b320d-266f-4772-b2d0-7b7aa9333f4b", "type": "concept", "title": "Floor plans and circulation"}, {"id": "72b5bf94-c78f-4fe5-9873-f0005255e72a", "type": "concept", "title": "Sight lines, thresholds, and pacing"}, {"id": "b4e4bc36-234d-467b-bd29-77f7a6a77663", "type": "concept", "title": "Light, sound, projection, and atmosphere"}, {"id": "62988441-8b71-48ed-b2cb-0b3df8d719b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Multi-part works and spatial rhythm"}], "description": "Students learn to orchestrate how viewers enter, move, pause, look, listen, and exit."}, {"id": "0261f0b3-76dc-41f3-985d-ad172226e94a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Site-Specific and Public Work", "children": [{"id": "0bebf6b0-cf17-43e5-a911-68ed522679ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Site research and mapping"}, {"id": "002bd011-c49a-4916-a620-be6f64e869f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Architecture, landscape, and history"}, {"id": "0d85dbf5-519b-4d82-82a2-562b984f4c9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Public permissions and stakeholders"}, {"id": "7d8bdc63-d6d4-4124-850a-d0348a0fde6a", "type": "concept", "title": "Weather, durability, maintenance, and safety"}], "description": "The point is to understand that place is not a backdrop; it is part of the sculpture."}, {"id": "20f10863-e671-48f7-afe8-19a9f5672072", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social and Participatory Practice", "children": [{"id": "aded5d42-67ab-4204-9b2c-3d26a49eb654", "type": "concept", "title": "Audience participation and consent"}, {"id": "acde9b42-a5d9-4129-a166-0fa1369e5d24", "type": "concept", "title": "Community research and accountability"}, {"id": "2cf3a6bb-f560-4c15-aa01-69ead91bd347", "type": "concept", "title": "Documentation of ephemeral work"}, {"id": "f6ebf10e-ad14-49c0-8706-ef697c44d345", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethics of collaboration and representation"}], "description": "Students learn how sculpture can operate as event, collaboration, service, protest, or community encounter."}]}, {"id": "aa253d74-68d7-4e90-8b1e-a184eedf3382", "type": "topic", "title": "Digital Modeling, 3D Scanning, CNC/Laser/3D Printing, and Hybrid Fabrication", "description": "Digital tools expand what sculptors can model, test, fabricate, and document. Students learn to combine hand processes with precise digital workflows without letting software flatten artistic judgment.", "children": [{"id": "ce808bfa-cc38-4358-b800-3a0d264d0888", "type": "subtopic", "title": "3D Modeling and Visualization", "children": [{"id": "3530c56d-94e5-4edd-82d8-780820e53a17", "type": "concept", "title": "Rhino, SketchUp, and mesh/NURBS concepts"}, {"id": "f3cbe058-2db1-42c3-b2b2-3b2da87305a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Orthographic views and measurements"}, {"id": "91dae90e-123c-4b83-bb66-d3751af81e31", "type": "concept", "title": "Rendering and material previews"}, {"id": "8e02351b-c122-411f-8e6f-031389455c7a", "type": "concept", "title": "Exporting files for fabrication"}], "description": "Students use digital modeling to test scale, form, installation, and fabrication before committing material resources."}, {"id": "46e4082b-b51b-46cd-a75a-3af3663a6789", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scanning, CNC, Laser, and 3D Printing", "children": [{"id": "6818602a-fbbc-4f15-ba65-e7e18e410cfc", "type": "concept", "title": "3D scanning and mesh cleanup"}, {"id": "163433e5-63f0-47d9-a61c-46803b56c76e", "type": "concept", "title": "CNC routing and tool paths overview"}, {"id": "3e64822d-d701-4209-9125-5d571673a411", "type": "concept", "title": "Laser cutting and kerf planning"}, {"id": "242eb22f-8113-4ee8-91ab-c9fddb5d0a0d", "type": "concept", "title": "3D printing supports, tolerances, and post-processing"}], "description": "The gist is learning where digital fabrication is powerful and where it needs hand finishing or structural correction."}, {"id": "ef1a9551-8252-47f7-90e8-a0268f5c0ab9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Hybrid Fabrication", "children": [{"id": "0293f15c-59f4-4618-a554-388e5f9cbbd7", "type": "concept", "title": "Digital maquettes and physical mockups"}, {"id": "956189bc-aa4d-4881-abe9-41fcbc1e5acd", "type": "concept", "title": "File naming and version control"}, {"id": "93442441-0b3c-4cca-b8a1-874a654a068c", "type": "concept", "title": "Combining printed, cast, carved, and found parts"}, {"id": "eef2788f-0810-4ee8-b22c-5e56129ec4fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Failure testing and tolerance adjustment"}], "description": "Students learn to move between screen, shop, and gallery through iterative prototypes."}]}, {"id": "1508468a-c452-4f12-8cc3-ac4db5585162", "type": "topic", "title": "Surface, Finish, Color, Patina, Texture, and Conservation Awareness", "description": "Surface is not decoration after the fact; it affects touch, time, durability, light, and interpretation. Students learn to finish work intentionally and understand basic conservation consequences.", "children": [{"id": "52abe57e-493b-435a-a3f0-840f255d19fd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Color, Paint, and Patina", "children": [{"id": "fb4a0ce0-ce7f-4f96-bb29-dea484a55619", "type": "concept", "title": "Primers, paints, stains, dyes, and pigments"}, {"id": "c9758d34-6150-46c8-b391-1f541bf564c2", "type": "concept", "title": "Metal oxidation and patina basics"}, {"id": "7b70e6bb-8618-46ed-9534-2dd46ae461e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Color systems and spatial effects"}, {"id": "e65d667d-2f88-4f56-8571-ed0bff3d0396", "type": "concept", "title": "Testing finish samples"}], "description": "Students learn how color and patina can unify parts, disguise construction, reveal process, or change historical associations."}, {"id": "819bb141-8dee-4b63-9811-6d27d13df753", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Texture and Tactility", "children": [{"id": "7d6185fa-de93-477d-8cba-1933a1b25818", "type": "concept", "title": "Polished, matte, rough, porous, and reflective surfaces"}, {"id": "3b31c2f9-c1b8-42d9-b2fa-c29bc6d4419f", "type": "concept", "title": "Tool marks and handmade evidence"}, {"id": "bacb9bd7-ffa1-49e1-bd29-72b6674ca83a", "type": "concept", "title": "Applied skins, coatings, and veneers"}, {"id": "119e1847-4fc4-4bf1-9e14-5ede2cdaee1b", "type": "concept", "title": "Texture as metaphor and material fact"}], "description": "The point is to understand how surface invites or refuses touch and how texture changes light."}, {"id": "90cad117-262e-4691-a700-028d2eeb1368", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Durability and Conservation Awareness", "children": [{"id": "731aea91-2a57-4a34-b90a-cd5574f9a36b", "type": "concept", "title": "Archival versus temporary choices"}, {"id": "138f8c97-43ae-4038-b78d-4615bf7a0146", "type": "concept", "title": "Compatibility between materials"}, {"id": "02456d5a-458d-4446-8748-ffa76b84fb7a", "type": "concept", "title": "Cleaning and repair records"}, {"id": "4c347da7-c0ea-4707-a58f-8fc89cc56347", "type": "concept", "title": "Storage, packing, and maintenance instructions"}], "description": "Students learn to anticipate aging, cracking, fading, rust, pests, water, ultraviolet exposure, and handling damage."}]}, {"id": "fc379c50-a870-4fa1-a40b-22562c6c379b", "type": "topic", "title": "Sculptural Traditions, Contemporary Sculpture, and Critical Theory", "description": "This unit situates studio work within long, contested histories. Students study sculptural traditions and contemporary theory so their work can enter larger conversations with intelligence.", "children": [{"id": "b7c85872-40bf-49a4-9b1a-2db8bf9a58e9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Historical Traditions", "children": [{"id": "df82f216-bf4e-4ca5-a534-78fb167c5f2a", "type": "concept", "title": "Ancient, classical, indigenous, African, Asian, European, and American examples"}, {"id": "e8240c11-ac53-43f5-bb86-580e4fae5ed7", "type": "concept", "title": "Ritual, memorial, religious, and civic functions"}, {"id": "56345f84-31ea-4c47-a98c-a3539eea6a73", "type": "concept", "title": "Materials and patronage"}, {"id": "2df702fd-026f-4767-8ead-d9958d6e04a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Museum display and colonial collecting histories"}], "description": "Students build a broad reference base across cultures, functions, materials, monuments, ritual objects, and museum histories."}, {"id": "fd6ac2ff-1dd6-499b-aebb-2ed73ffca635", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Modern and Contemporary Sculpture", "children": [{"id": "7d3f3a45-2dc2-457a-a7ce-995ab92c39e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Modernism and the expanded field"}, {"id": "bd54685a-b61e-4381-8128-ffa3bce42e9c", "type": "concept", "title": "Minimalism and postminimalism"}, {"id": "b6c58495-e87c-48f1-96d7-f645de0d8c45", "type": "concept", "title": "Feminist, queer, and decolonial sculpture"}, {"id": "cf92821f-d293-4eb1-9b0f-19fcba559084", "type": "concept", "title": "Ecology, technology, and global contemporary practice"}], "description": "The gist is understanding how sculpture changed through abstraction, industrial materials, minimalism, installation, performance, and new media."}, {"id": "6678ce21-b481-40ef-a737-179c965099db", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critical Theory for Makers", "children": [{"id": "2c437bd7-0bf1-4045-8ddb-fabcc868f2b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Phenomenology and embodiment"}, {"id": "1406aec8-2c03-4549-a07b-9c64e396178b", "type": "concept", "title": "Semiotics and material culture"}, {"id": "40cd555d-e211-4a2f-af1b-94dd377f7fee", "type": "concept", "title": "Institutional critique"}, {"id": "5f3a5762-808a-4a1b-856a-583464a6e969", "type": "concept", "title": "More-than-human, ecological, and networked thinking"}], "description": "Students learn useful theory as studio equipment, not as decorative vocabulary."}]}, {"id": "162997a9-9ca6-416c-b188-3fa8643ed8f0", "type": "topic", "title": "Critique, Documentation, Artist Statements, and Portfolio Development", "description": "Sculpture must be made, discussed, photographed, written about, and remembered. This unit builds habits for critique, documentation, statements, and portfolio development.", "children": [{"id": "78c6d416-1563-4b7f-b4c2-bab14fa66a31", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critique Methods", "children": [{"id": "cdac0e94-d2c1-49c3-8da2-3447c0a106f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Description before judgment"}, {"id": "6569082b-ea6c-4cf5-9a2b-6c24a54b16e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Formal, material, conceptual, and contextual critique"}, {"id": "ef81a686-1797-476f-872c-4b5b3a0f67ed", "type": "concept", "title": "Questions, evidence, and revision paths"}, {"id": "8d796f7a-1372-4e69-a9b8-87c7440c1913", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer review and self-assessment"}], "description": "Students learn to give and receive precise, generous, rigorous feedback that can change the work."}, {"id": "b41dab26-30ee-4c4e-af07-c963fd4ffb15", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Documentation", "children": [{"id": "2e2efa01-1f5e-43e8-8f9c-a99235902090", "type": "concept", "title": "Lighting and background choices"}, {"id": "2cba22e1-d6d3-4745-9a9a-8902e8c2a512", "type": "concept", "title": "Scale figures and detail shots"}, {"id": "6a1cb157-11e0-4cfb-bc5f-853d383d9742", "type": "concept", "title": "Video walkthroughs and process images"}, {"id": "c1f58e59-f60b-490b-b047-ce5f67cfeeb0", "type": "concept", "title": "File organization and metadata"}], "description": "The point is to preserve spatial work through photographs, video, diagrams, captions, and installation records."}, {"id": "f29b3502-73cd-4b84-a7ed-12b17ca1a115", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Artist Statements and Portfolio", "children": [{"id": "9c044f38-b1d4-4c55-8708-d8e414d83325", "type": "concept", "title": "Short statements and project descriptions"}, {"id": "281843a8-064e-40d1-8843-c4db64019327", "type": "concept", "title": "Material lists and dimensions"}, {"id": "0fd0aabf-d8ef-4fff-a673-e98db6e6a08f", "type": "concept", "title": "Portfolio sequencing and captions"}, {"id": "4609973f-f045-4142-bec4-bf111819e621", "type": "concept", "title": "CV, website, and application readiness"}], "description": "Students learn to make writing support the work without overexplaining it."}]}, {"id": "aefd2d20-ba05-40a5-b41d-5d35d28fa200", "type": "topic", "title": "Exhibition Design, Accessibility, Installation Safety, Rights, and Deinstallation", "description": "Exhibition planning turns finished work into a responsible public encounter. Students learn to install with attention to accessibility, hardware, labels, rights, audience safety, and deinstallation.", "children": [{"id": "9172cc3c-2193-4d3f-97ac-e8b7615e77fc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Exhibition Layout and Accessibility", "children": [{"id": "373d214e-9a96-4649-bf7a-98904f3c1a86", "type": "concept", "title": "Floor plans and object spacing"}, {"id": "7816bdc4-5137-47df-ba81-502332f1c6ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessible routes and viewing heights"}, {"id": "4e7ea90d-7152-4e93-ac2d-5c087d79967d", "type": "concept", "title": "Lighting, sound, projection, and sensory load"}, {"id": "d2fb02de-31eb-4863-849c-2768162f4f12", "type": "concept", "title": "Labels, wall text, and plain-language access"}], "description": "Students learn to design displays that respect bodies, movement, visibility, sensory access, and interpretive clarity."}, {"id": "24713b7f-8c3f-4518-b230-3f9111b46043", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Installation Safety and Rights", "children": [{"id": "c5eb7604-3fc3-433a-87e2-680a617696a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Anchoring, suspension, pedestals, barriers, and load limits"}, {"id": "d714a501-5ce7-4c9c-a1c8-cab9b953f99d", "type": "concept", "title": "Electrical, trip, sharp-edge, and fire concerns"}, {"id": "90826fb8-538a-4c51-bd80-2f73de4d6d98", "type": "concept", "title": "Image, sound, object, and participant permissions"}, {"id": "1cd2dc89-c10b-4d32-b9c9-bbba56440854", "type": "concept", "title": "Insurance, loan forms, and condition reports overview"}], "description": "The gist is to prevent harm and professionalize the practical details that make exhibitions possible."}, {"id": "4c305beb-41b5-4d9c-927c-79b3922d4e94", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Maintenance and Deinstallation", "children": [{"id": "7dfbb2a3-dec6-47cc-8c92-a78a27b7f6c9", "type": "concept", "title": "Checklists and installation manuals"}, {"id": "45fc8c6a-248d-4ea2-a695-c1d91323a70d", "type": "concept", "title": "Maintenance schedules"}, {"id": "25375fd4-863b-46ad-995b-48f029373411", "type": "concept", "title": "Packing, labeling, and storage"}, {"id": "3a3cf95f-e102-4f3d-b1ec-fc013a82173d", "type": "concept", "title": "Deinstallation, recycling, and waste planning"}], "description": "Students learn that the life of the work includes upkeep, removal, storage, disposal, and archive."}]}, {"id": "36d83f7a-50b7-4725-885c-58991a9fb127", "type": "topic", "title": "Capstone Sculpture Studio: Proposal, Prototype, Fabricate, Install, Reflect", "description": "The capstone asks students to synthesize research, design, fabrication, installation, critique, and reflection into a coherent sculptural project with professional documentation.", "children": [{"id": "0d8a6e03-d8a5-4d5a-8300-6d83990328d8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Proposal and Research", "children": [{"id": "215aa7b1-f6f9-4aea-8ba4-9fea3de0558e", "type": "concept", "title": "Concept statement and research images"}, {"id": "590c6a30-30e4-4e9e-aa1f-2d54a760d010", "type": "concept", "title": "Material tests and budget"}, {"id": "0bc49168-0659-49d0-94cb-2b86777d0786", "type": "concept", "title": "Timeline and fabrication sequence"}, {"id": "82d81de2-29fe-4d5a-a13b-9f9f84f6aa2a", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety and installation plan"}], "description": "Students learn to turn ambition into a feasible plan with references, materials, budget, timeline, and risk assessment."}, {"id": "b18918e8-7915-47db-90fb-83a0dbcc6f92", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Prototype, Fabricate, Revise", "children": [{"id": "daa85391-7c05-4aad-a2a7-d2f50390bbb8", "type": "concept", "title": "Maquettes and mockups"}, {"id": "9b753747-a77a-42dd-bf07-e95a0f6e8c3e", "type": "concept", "title": "Material tests and structural tests"}, {"id": "43bd9e9f-af96-4314-8e78-3f3a092dcd1d", "type": "concept", "title": "Critique-based revisions"}, {"id": "5b22c8bd-ecdc-45af-8c37-b3ce9015e7f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Finishing and quality control"}], "description": "The point is to make strategically: test early, fail usefully, revise visibly, and solve problems before final installation."}, {"id": "af2c5022-bb0b-450d-9916-009d6691d76d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Install, Reflect, and Archive", "children": [{"id": "c7e0f69e-2f32-4b9c-b0c0-184b3a57303d", "type": "concept", "title": "Final installation and viewer experience"}, {"id": "e2215027-f499-4d83-a90d-3acab8415990", "type": "concept", "title": "Documentation portfolio"}, {"id": "42d3c466-0bbc-40e4-b322-6ddcb052db90", "type": "concept", "title": "Artist statement and reflection"}, {"id": "2c449192-d2c1-4d67-ab94-9980561f511a", "type": "concept", "title": "Archive, storage, or deinstallation plan"}], "description": "Students complete the project by presenting it well and learning from the evidence of process."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$sculjson$::jsonb,
  true,
  false,
  'course',
  'public'
where not exists (
  select 1 from public.learning_paths where slug = 'sculpture'
);

update public.learning_paths
set
  title = 'Sculpture',
  goal = 'Sculpture',
  summary = 'This course introduces sculpture as a material, spatial, conceptual, and social practice. Students learn foundational 3-D design, additive and subtractive processes, construction, casting, assemblage, installation, site-specific practice, digital fabrication, critique, documentation, and professional exhibition methods. The course balances technical skill, material intelligence, historical literacy, contemporary theory, and ambitious studio production.',
  data = $sculjson${"slug": "sculpture", "title": "Sculpture", "description": "This course introduces sculpture as a material, spatial, conceptual, and social practice. Students learn foundational 3-D design, additive and subtractive processes, construction, casting, assemblage, installation, site-specific practice, digital fabrication, critique, documentation, and professional exhibition methods. The course balances technical skill, material intelligence, historical literacy, contemporary theory, and ambitious studio production.", "topics": [{"id": "f05c29af-eded-4876-95bb-08c74437841d", "type": "topic", "title": "Sculpture as Object, Space, Material, and Experience", "description": "This opening unit frames sculpture as more than an object. Students learn to think across material presence, spatial placement, viewer movement, historical reference, and lived experience.", "children": [{"id": "92464d2a-7215-433d-a6b7-72b3b35e63fc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Object and Thingness", "children": [{"id": "2e1ba199-c89f-4f8d-808e-bf33f55d968a", "type": "concept", "title": "Objecthood and material presence"}, {"id": "09c10986-2954-4309-a293-192aa5cc192a", "type": "concept", "title": "Autonomy versus context"}, {"id": "3763837c-1cb8-4f70-ab9c-6244581d389f", "type": "concept", "title": "Pedestals, supports, and display conventions"}, {"id": "6998a1e8-cce4-4e5f-8704-ca61d12c3a4f", "type": "concept", "title": "Touch, proximity, and bodily scale"}], "description": "Students learn why sculptural meaning begins with physical presence: weight, surface, size, resistance, orientation, and how an object occupies attention."}, {"id": "7166ef05-f741-4697-bf1a-3701c8b32f0f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Space and Viewer Experience", "children": [{"id": "fffa32ee-df14-4769-8628-fe3c9eb17916", "type": "concept", "title": "Frontality and all-around viewing"}, {"id": "6d061c77-20be-4b29-8d2e-6d73cd2dab25", "type": "concept", "title": "Sight lines and circulation"}, {"id": "e85ca964-086d-44d5-9780-f08f1380d9d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Void, interval, and negative space"}, {"id": "056295ad-d647-4352-90f3-3ce8f737571e", "type": "concept", "title": "Temporal experience and sequence"}], "description": "The point is to see sculpture as something encountered through movement rather than absorbed from a single fixed viewpoint."}, {"id": "0135cc58-930d-432f-bd22-e51154732fe1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Concept, Context, and Encounter", "children": [{"id": "6b36cf25-04ff-48ef-bb73-52243def2c1e", "type": "concept", "title": "Site and institutional context"}, {"id": "48441443-b54f-48c1-bc01-45586be456be", "type": "concept", "title": "Narrative, symbol, and metaphor"}, {"id": "d3205542-1517-4a12-859e-7ffd500fd908", "type": "concept", "title": "Embodiment and phenomenology"}, {"id": "0008ea9a-94c8-4033-9cca-792aa8ba64ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Audience, participation, and interpretation"}], "description": "Students connect formal choices to ideas, locations, histories, and audiences so that making decisions carry intellectual force."}]}, {"id": "8b031c1a-5d88-4900-b144-f6961b55f203", "type": "topic", "title": "Three-Dimensional Design: Form, Volume, Mass, Scale, and Space", "description": "This unit builds the visual grammar of 3-D work. Students learn to compose with form, mass, volume, scale, proportion, gravity, and spatial relationships before committing to complex materials.", "children": [{"id": "0bd1d0fe-2242-40cd-830b-5101da26bfa7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Form, Volume, and Mass", "children": [{"id": "5ed7dc4b-4ced-4304-b305-3bbfa27d145c", "type": "concept", "title": "Geometric and organic form"}, {"id": "73e0bb8e-8356-4cfa-8582-7e03292cba45", "type": "concept", "title": "Solid mass versus implied volume"}, {"id": "b6453db6-3217-42c6-b5cd-9493668de070", "type": "concept", "title": "Positive and negative space"}, {"id": "bba820f9-d6d6-4674-a50c-97ec8e3eeae7", "type": "concept", "title": "Proportion, rhythm, and repetition"}], "description": "Students develop control over the basic sculptural elements that make an object feel light, dense, dynamic, stable, compressed, or expansive."}, {"id": "55424d1c-3b2b-4984-af10-2526d485dd06", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scale and Human Reference", "children": [{"id": "e6c4371d-9bfd-42c4-9632-9e4e1907765f", "type": "concept", "title": "Maquettes and scale models"}, {"id": "b1725d14-4f4e-4e4e-8dcb-7a8d9f2825e1", "type": "concept", "title": "Body scale and ergonomic reference"}, {"id": "6f8df4b2-7cf4-4eb3-ba4d-b28cdbe6e99d", "type": "concept", "title": "Monumentality and intimacy"}, {"id": "d0a5dda0-30fc-49f0-ae68-a4fb6dfacecd", "type": "concept", "title": "Measurement, enlargement, and translation"}], "description": "The gist is learning how scale changes meaning, from hand-held object to architectural intervention to public monument."}, {"id": "baec9511-d1b8-4be3-b769-95f5ea651ccb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Balance, Gravity, and Spatial Tension", "children": [{"id": "f157a4f8-b8f3-4b17-84b3-865d22cbf919", "type": "concept", "title": "Center of gravity"}, {"id": "74652923-57b8-48f5-92de-825ff70cb328", "type": "concept", "title": "Cantilever and counterweight"}, {"id": "c604b5cb-ac18-4c41-bf13-41e7ba79bb05", "type": "concept", "title": "Symmetry and asymmetry"}, {"id": "a5d996a7-22ea-4cef-bbdf-e1bcdda8fadc", "type": "concept", "title": "Visual tension versus physical stability"}], "description": "Students learn that sculpture must persuade both the eye and the body; it has to look intentional and often has to stand safely."}]}, {"id": "64988136-2eae-43a7-88c6-733d11754df4", "type": "topic", "title": "Materials, Tools, Studio Safety, and Shop Literacy", "description": "A world-class sculpture course treats safety and shop literacy as creative infrastructure. Students learn to choose materials intelligently, handle tools responsibly, and plan work before risks accumulate.", "children": [{"id": "be755742-0fb4-4f7d-be5c-7c6dd0f3017f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Material Families and Properties", "children": [{"id": "518703fb-92ab-4911-a15c-e6c790b665ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Clay, plaster, wood, metal, foam, plastics, textiles"}, {"id": "d6784ac9-caf0-4083-b67a-a7cfec67c31d", "type": "concept", "title": "Structural and surface properties"}, {"id": "1fe7636a-48e2-45f4-8503-9ab0da6ac347", "type": "concept", "title": "Archival and temporary materials"}, {"id": "e9f7dad8-8f53-4ca9-aec2-9cc300eb876a", "type": "concept", "title": "Material tests and sample boards"}], "description": "Students compare materials by strength, flexibility, weight, toxicity, workability, cost, durability, and expressive potential."}, {"id": "197ad5c7-9084-4f85-9c6a-3e3e3dad7aae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Tool Use and Shop Workflow", "children": [{"id": "9ad2c71f-017a-49c3-8474-bac36087afae", "type": "concept", "title": "Hand tools and power tools"}, {"id": "5e1a2cf2-1169-4057-a235-316077e9d694", "type": "concept", "title": "Clamps, vises, jigs, and fixtures"}, {"id": "7ae9d1e8-daf8-4582-8314-7cb5c2e9a778", "type": "concept", "title": "Measuring, marking, cutting, and assembly"}, {"id": "8079811b-ce93-4b2a-82cf-00d03b656b1e", "type": "concept", "title": "Maintenance, storage, and cleanup routines"}], "description": "The point is to make students more independent in the studio while respecting shared equipment and time."}, {"id": "a46ad3c8-440b-47b8-91af-8dd1c2117f2d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Safety, Risk, and Documentation", "children": [{"id": "a73ff11f-4fde-42b3-9cd0-3fd9c7441c00", "type": "concept", "title": "Personal protective equipment"}, {"id": "b891efcd-38ff-4164-91b7-98e81dedcb75", "type": "concept", "title": "Ventilation, dust, solvents, and fumes"}, {"id": "d4e66dca-9898-4c64-a04e-113ecc1de892", "type": "concept", "title": "Material safety data sheets"}, {"id": "9bab3649-b5d3-4752-b419-1525b2e60037", "type": "concept", "title": "Lifting, transport, and emergency procedures"}], "description": "Students learn to make risk visible before they cut, cast, weld, sand, spray, lift, or install."}]}, {"id": "08dc9974-d480-4f74-9534-b287798010a2", "type": "topic", "title": "Additive Modeling: Clay, Wax, Plaster, Armatures, and Figure Construction", "description": "Additive modeling develops the hand, eye, and ability to build form gradually. Students work from gesture and mass toward structure, anatomy, surface, and expressive refinement.", "children": [{"id": "64eebbb4-71eb-4608-99da-9fc12d08de66", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Clay, Wax, and Plaster Modeling", "children": [{"id": "aa2a6400-ba54-47e2-9ced-d214d85d935d", "type": "concept", "title": "Coils, slabs, modeling, and joining"}, {"id": "0063d9f4-40eb-4634-a144-fff073813b8d", "type": "concept", "title": "Wax modeling and repair"}, {"id": "05b5c02a-202c-4162-ab53-ca34649306b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Plaster buildup and carving back"}, {"id": "d5e6b2fc-6f79-47c1-a9e1-4f31cba72e0a", "type": "concept", "title": "Drying, curing, and cracking control"}], "description": "Students learn materials that invite revision, compression, addition, and expressive touch."}, {"id": "0a28038a-6a08-4fd6-8e67-e90432d94da1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Armatures and Internal Support", "children": [{"id": "66fe3f13-ec07-4a9a-9fb7-4c19eb5d0d3b", "type": "concept", "title": "Wire, pipe, wood, and mixed armatures"}, {"id": "82e60471-d95d-4c5f-b7c7-3f4861e876aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Load, balance, and anchor points"}, {"id": "e5212dd5-6894-4d8f-b35b-391a4231e5aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Removable versus embedded supports"}, {"id": "7501dd60-9bb6-4c42-909b-5b261cb10b2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Compatibility with clay, plaster, and casting"}], "description": "The gist is learning that hidden structure shapes what the surface can do."}, {"id": "b1dd393f-84e6-4e68-aecd-01373fda5125", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Figure, Gesture, and Surface", "children": [{"id": "48909b4f-91d0-42d7-a9bc-30be7737ee87", "type": "concept", "title": "Gesture and pose"}, {"id": "5193f3b6-d749-4207-bc6a-fd3542659c7d", "type": "concept", "title": "Proportion and skeletal landmarks"}, {"id": "58e5f797-1b7a-4f4f-8342-2a7591d55677", "type": "concept", "title": "Plane changes and anatomy overview"}, {"id": "951f83d3-159e-408f-88a6-790472026314", "type": "concept", "title": "Texture, tool marks, and finish"}], "description": "Students learn how body-based observation strengthens both representational and abstract sculpture."}]}, {"id": "7584b66a-2a78-49d3-95dd-fe523edd9618", "type": "topic", "title": "Subtractive Processes: Carving, Cutting, Shaping, and Surface", "description": "Subtractive methods teach commitment, patience, and the intelligence of removal. Students learn how form emerges through cutting, carving, sanding, scraping, and surface decisions.", "children": [{"id": "b2181331-c9d0-437e-82f6-f4c23ebbfc6f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Carving Logic", "children": [{"id": "58dcdc81-466e-4c11-968e-abfd28bd1116", "type": "concept", "title": "Block planning and profile drawings"}, {"id": "30656c5f-7f64-477d-91d2-9ac11a8c69eb", "type": "concept", "title": "Roughing, refining, and finishing"}, {"id": "99ac64ae-e9a7-42f3-a9c5-40fc880531d9", "type": "concept", "title": "Grain, direction, and fracture"}, {"id": "8015d103-e6f9-4705-a2d4-66a8de37f432", "type": "concept", "title": "Relief versus freestanding carving"}], "description": "Students learn to think from the outside inward, preserving what matters while removing what does not."}, {"id": "4971a7e1-c691-4c30-a934-03a9b007358e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Materials for Subtractive Work", "children": [{"id": "a9e166dd-c16c-4059-9a40-a7ca5f747e59", "type": "concept", "title": "Foam and plaster blocks"}, {"id": "bcb56d8e-6c5f-4cd2-b9d1-7aec536a58b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Wood species and grain behavior"}, {"id": "931a67b2-f603-40d5-9385-4f4da6845c83", "type": "concept", "title": "Stone overview and tool limits"}, {"id": "9da83b98-e931-44a7-aa7b-4b10acf31db3", "type": "concept", "title": "Composite and reclaimed materials"}], "description": "The point is to match tool, material, and ambition so the process is feasible and expressive."}, {"id": "24e55257-9857-423c-85b5-1f295f978772", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Surface and Edge Control", "children": [{"id": "330d32ee-21c5-4e8a-aad8-00aa6959203d", "type": "concept", "title": "Rasps, files, chisels, knives, and sandpaper"}, {"id": "bb80d6d6-e7d0-4c1c-b936-2d6c6588d3b9", "type": "concept", "title": "Edge sharpness and softness"}, {"id": "604a8bd2-e923-4ee1-b1ef-f53672e9160b", "type": "concept", "title": "Texture as evidence of process"}, {"id": "332bc089-b60d-4335-8e92-eaca3e1ba938", "type": "concept", "title": "Sealing, polishing, painting, and repair"}], "description": "Students learn that carving is not finished when the shape appears; surface is part of the idea."}]}, {"id": "ae6cff81-77ce-4dd4-85ce-6b0ee38199ca", "type": "topic", "title": "Construction: Wood, Metal, Fasteners, Welding, Joinery, and Structural Logic", "description": "Construction joins separate parts into a sculptural whole. Students learn structural thinking, fabrication sequencing, material compatibility, and the difference between a joint that merely holds and one that contributes meaning.", "children": [{"id": "5cfd8224-f777-4ce3-9f64-13d6c25ac8ae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Wood and Joinery", "children": [{"id": "63f97fcc-c83c-4ceb-91ee-42f38c913614", "type": "concept", "title": "Measuring, cutting, drilling, and sanding"}, {"id": "8fbf6975-52ce-4d9f-9faf-d40134911adc", "type": "concept", "title": "Butt, lap, miter, and dowel joints"}, {"id": "9b7da7a2-8fbc-4f45-bcee-2ec1bd1a947a", "type": "concept", "title": "Screws, bolts, glue, and clamps"}, {"id": "fefd2402-1aef-4afd-875a-3233ebf12664", "type": "concept", "title": "Frames, boxes, bases, and armatures"}], "description": "Students learn basic woodworking as a foundation for frames, supports, pedestals, and finished sculptural forms."}, {"id": "e1141d64-ef73-4b69-9a2b-528e41d78e7f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Metal and Welding Overview", "children": [{"id": "a9590fe3-88fb-4572-988c-01732a75a71b", "type": "concept", "title": "Cutting, grinding, drilling, and bending"}, {"id": "f34a2d16-893a-4e92-9485-14b52417d58e", "type": "concept", "title": "Welding concepts and shop protocols"}, {"id": "4a0d3990-f799-4b12-842d-08dd748b7e20", "type": "concept", "title": "Fasteners and mechanical connections"}, {"id": "a5b3797c-daba-4364-a0ff-db9e160389be", "type": "concept", "title": "Rust, patina, paint, and finish"}], "description": "The gist is to understand metal as line, mass, structure, and surface, with strong attention to supervised safety."}, {"id": "853d1868-1d0c-4a3c-89b2-4306a057ae5f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Structural Logic and Fabrication Plans", "children": [{"id": "25b56cb7-3c45-4829-9c6b-1b1aa70e8c93", "type": "concept", "title": "Load paths and stress points"}, {"id": "ca89c8af-4e79-4d2b-8ac2-8ae642427886", "type": "concept", "title": "Modular construction and disassembly"}, {"id": "fdd0adcf-9005-4b2d-b2c1-d6dd6df2f90c", "type": "concept", "title": "Templates, jigs, and mockups"}, {"id": "8dfdf7a5-1061-42f0-a818-2bd3d8ec9aad", "type": "concept", "title": "Transport, storage, and installation constraints"}], "description": "Students learn to design the making process before the final object fails or becomes impossible to transport."}]}, {"id": "b51c5ebb-0327-4af3-ba2d-3887ec834b9b", "type": "topic", "title": "Casting and Moldmaking: Plaster, Resin, Rubber, Bronze Overview, and Multiples", "description": "Casting and moldmaking introduce replication, translation, and transformation. Students learn how a form can move across materials, scales, editions, and levels of finish.", "children": [{"id": "deda63f9-e31e-4f43-bbec-583ed0b216b3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mold Types and Planning", "children": [{"id": "27df011f-cdc1-4a89-bba6-6ff78df1ca40", "type": "concept", "title": "One-part and two-part molds"}, {"id": "8f89713d-3e9d-4fa0-bdb3-cf91e59193e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Flexible rubber molds"}, {"id": "41797108-3073-441c-8642-9688e491eb2a", "type": "concept", "title": "Keys, registration, and release agents"}, {"id": "43d1047e-3386-4dc6-bce4-63d170bc0bd1", "type": "concept", "title": "Undercuts, vents, and pour gates"}], "description": "Students learn that mold design is sculptural problem-solving: every undercut, seam, key, and pour path matters."}, {"id": "a003b408-da4a-40f7-8866-d861ead4a85e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Casting Materials and Processes", "children": [{"id": "11da7daa-aa4b-41ca-9d29-45f547a55c81", "type": "concept", "title": "Plaster, cement, wax, resin, and slip overview"}, {"id": "824f8c33-81cc-49bf-893b-38e5a23b796b", "type": "concept", "title": "Mixing ratios and cure times"}, {"id": "5af3c223-080a-48fd-8f69-fa5e45a6fea3", "type": "concept", "title": "Colorants, fillers, and inclusions"}, {"id": "78ada06a-3625-4ec8-af34-cf2eede4761b", "type": "concept", "title": "Defects, bubbles, repairs, and cleanup"}], "description": "The point is to understand how different casting materials behave and what each adds to meaning."}, {"id": "b76809d7-aa60-4169-b671-0e4e196b0fe3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Editions, Multiples, and Bronze Overview", "children": [{"id": "1cdda518-d77e-4883-89a9-3f3b19e1442d", "type": "concept", "title": "Editioning and record keeping"}, {"id": "7ee0f313-0796-466b-9780-0d4637c0780e", "type": "concept", "title": "Lost-wax bronze concepts"}, {"id": "3bde1525-ed2c-4ab3-9c62-a1ab387f407a", "type": "concept", "title": "Foundry collaboration and safety"}, {"id": "fcf6f890-d1a4-4ce6-acd2-67b046e4283a", "type": "concept", "title": "Multiples, series, and installation strategies"}], "description": "Students learn casting as a way to think about repetition, variation, value, and professional production."}]}, {"id": "c1707b26-f30e-43fc-bb0e-307354939c46", "type": "topic", "title": "Assemblage, Found Objects, Mixed Media, and Readymade Strategies", "description": "Assemblage and found-object work sharpen selection, context, and juxtaposition. Students learn how existing materials carry histories and how composition can redirect those histories.", "children": [{"id": "03a46747-9636-4c26-b19a-d58bb7ca3829", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Readymade and Object Selection", "children": [{"id": "4de8f4b5-ff37-4564-94c7-1de20433c8df", "type": "concept", "title": "Duchamp and readymade traditions"}, {"id": "2fa6664f-125a-44ca-8c67-162959752171", "type": "concept", "title": "Commodity, tool, archive, and relic"}, {"id": "467a1b0c-3955-44ab-b7df-f6809767687c", "type": "concept", "title": "Humor, irony, and displacement"}, {"id": "91d401da-78a7-4312-b44a-8a5639270bfa", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethics of source, ownership, and representation"}], "description": "Students learn to see ordinary objects as carriers of use, class, labor, memory, design, and cultural meaning."}, {"id": "c9083c94-44f1-4844-a074-1aa957e5f0a5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Assemblage and Mixed Media", "children": [{"id": "ee2a8f23-4b6f-4b3b-92b5-e089cd9cbc46", "type": "concept", "title": "Accumulation and collage in space"}, {"id": "45476d9e-feae-4d7a-aae0-a6eb1913b9cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Fastening incompatible materials"}, {"id": "ffeddf98-614b-4175-84fc-8b2354403fb0", "type": "concept", "title": "Text, image, sound, light, and video elements"}, {"id": "5953f0c8-e3b7-4d10-a3e8-2552c37b2298", "type": "concept", "title": "Surface transitions and visual hierarchy"}], "description": "The gist is learning how unlike materials can hold together formally, structurally, and conceptually."}, {"id": "5fcc304d-a98c-4f9a-8c8d-deaf50cd18ab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Material Culture and Meaning", "children": [{"id": "a2563bbc-d816-45e1-9e91-4880ee0cf66e", "type": "concept", "title": "Domestic, industrial, and public objects"}, {"id": "d8dc4f54-d713-4c51-8283-99270a4ec4ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Memory, trauma, identity, and place"}, {"id": "0e873718-0836-475c-8c09-9ecdbc03c7af", "type": "concept", "title": "Waste, reuse, and environmental critique"}, {"id": "3aaea0e0-295e-4767-950d-242389d4c2d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Display as argument"}], "description": "Students learn to read objects socially, historically, politically, and personally."}]}, {"id": "1899a9ec-e1e5-4084-b3c9-049848771d7e", "type": "topic", "title": "Installation, Site-Specific, Public, and Socially Engaged Sculpture", "description": "This unit moves sculpture beyond the isolated studio object. Students learn to design for rooms, sites, institutions, publics, landscapes, communities, and viewer participation.", "children": [{"id": "4733812f-f458-4ec9-b169-c3441cf5a0fd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Installation and Spatial Sequence", "children": [{"id": "8c2b320d-266f-4772-b2d0-7b7aa9333f4b", "type": "concept", "title": "Floor plans and circulation"}, {"id": "72b5bf94-c78f-4fe5-9873-f0005255e72a", "type": "concept", "title": "Sight lines, thresholds, and pacing"}, {"id": "b4e4bc36-234d-467b-bd29-77f7a6a77663", "type": "concept", "title": "Light, sound, projection, and atmosphere"}, {"id": "62988441-8b71-48ed-b2cb-0b3df8d719b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Multi-part works and spatial rhythm"}], "description": "Students learn to orchestrate how viewers enter, move, pause, look, listen, and exit."}, {"id": "0261f0b3-76dc-41f3-985d-ad172226e94a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Site-Specific and Public Work", "children": [{"id": "0bebf6b0-cf17-43e5-a911-68ed522679ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Site research and mapping"}, {"id": "002bd011-c49a-4916-a620-be6f64e869f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Architecture, landscape, and history"}, {"id": "0d85dbf5-519b-4d82-82a2-562b984f4c9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Public permissions and stakeholders"}, {"id": "7d8bdc63-d6d4-4124-850a-d0348a0fde6a", "type": "concept", "title": "Weather, durability, maintenance, and safety"}], "description": "The point is to understand that place is not a backdrop; it is part of the sculpture."}, {"id": "20f10863-e671-48f7-afe8-19a9f5672072", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social and Participatory Practice", "children": [{"id": "aded5d42-67ab-4204-9b2c-3d26a49eb654", "type": "concept", "title": "Audience participation and consent"}, {"id": "acde9b42-a5d9-4129-a166-0fa1369e5d24", "type": "concept", "title": "Community research and accountability"}, {"id": "2cf3a6bb-f560-4c15-aa01-69ead91bd347", "type": "concept", "title": "Documentation of ephemeral work"}, {"id": "f6ebf10e-ad14-49c0-8706-ef697c44d345", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethics of collaboration and representation"}], "description": "Students learn how sculpture can operate as event, collaboration, service, protest, or community encounter."}]}, {"id": "aa253d74-68d7-4e90-8b1e-a184eedf3382", "type": "topic", "title": "Digital Modeling, 3D Scanning, CNC/Laser/3D Printing, and Hybrid Fabrication", "description": "Digital tools expand what sculptors can model, test, fabricate, and document. Students learn to combine hand processes with precise digital workflows without letting software flatten artistic judgment.", "children": [{"id": "ce808bfa-cc38-4358-b800-3a0d264d0888", "type": "subtopic", "title": "3D Modeling and Visualization", "children": [{"id": "3530c56d-94e5-4edd-82d8-780820e53a17", "type": "concept", "title": "Rhino, SketchUp, and mesh/NURBS concepts"}, {"id": "f3cbe058-2db1-42c3-b2b2-3b2da87305a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Orthographic views and measurements"}, {"id": "91dae90e-123c-4b83-bb66-d3751af81e31", "type": "concept", "title": "Rendering and material previews"}, {"id": "8e02351b-c122-411f-8e6f-031389455c7a", "type": "concept", "title": "Exporting files for fabrication"}], "description": "Students use digital modeling to test scale, form, installation, and fabrication before committing material resources."}, {"id": "46e4082b-b51b-46cd-a75a-3af3663a6789", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scanning, CNC, Laser, and 3D Printing", "children": [{"id": "6818602a-fbbc-4f15-ba65-e7e18e410cfc", "type": "concept", "title": "3D scanning and mesh cleanup"}, {"id": "163433e5-63f0-47d9-a61c-46803b56c76e", "type": "concept", "title": "CNC routing and tool paths overview"}, {"id": "3e64822d-d701-4209-9125-5d571673a411", "type": "concept", "title": "Laser cutting and kerf planning"}, {"id": "242eb22f-8113-4ee8-91ab-c9fddb5d0a0d", "type": "concept", "title": "3D printing supports, tolerances, and post-processing"}], "description": "The gist is learning where digital fabrication is powerful and where it needs hand finishing or structural correction."}, {"id": "ef1a9551-8252-47f7-90e8-a0268f5c0ab9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Hybrid Fabrication", "children": [{"id": "0293f15c-59f4-4618-a554-388e5f9cbbd7", "type": "concept", "title": "Digital maquettes and physical mockups"}, {"id": "956189bc-aa4d-4881-abe9-41fcbc1e5acd", "type": "concept", "title": "File naming and version control"}, {"id": "93442441-0b3c-4cca-b8a1-874a654a068c", "type": "concept", "title": "Combining printed, cast, carved, and found parts"}, {"id": "eef2788f-0810-4ee8-b22c-5e56129ec4fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Failure testing and tolerance adjustment"}], "description": "Students learn to move between screen, shop, and gallery through iterative prototypes."}]}, {"id": "1508468a-c452-4f12-8cc3-ac4db5585162", "type": "topic", "title": "Surface, Finish, Color, Patina, Texture, and Conservation Awareness", "description": "Surface is not decoration after the fact; it affects touch, time, durability, light, and interpretation. Students learn to finish work intentionally and understand basic conservation consequences.", "children": [{"id": "52abe57e-493b-435a-a3f0-840f255d19fd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Color, Paint, and Patina", "children": [{"id": "fb4a0ce0-ce7f-4f96-bb29-dea484a55619", "type": "concept", "title": "Primers, paints, stains, dyes, and pigments"}, {"id": "c9758d34-6150-46c8-b391-1f541bf564c2", "type": "concept", "title": "Metal oxidation and patina basics"}, {"id": "7b70e6bb-8618-46ed-9534-2dd46ae461e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Color systems and spatial effects"}, {"id": "e65d667d-2f88-4f56-8571-ed0bff3d0396", "type": "concept", "title": "Testing finish samples"}], "description": "Students learn how color and patina can unify parts, disguise construction, reveal process, or change historical associations."}, {"id": "819bb141-8dee-4b63-9811-6d27d13df753", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Texture and Tactility", "children": [{"id": "7d6185fa-de93-477d-8cba-1933a1b25818", "type": "concept", "title": "Polished, matte, rough, porous, and reflective surfaces"}, {"id": "3b31c2f9-c1b8-42d9-b2fa-c29bc6d4419f", "type": "concept", "title": "Tool marks and handmade evidence"}, {"id": "bacb9bd7-ffa1-49e1-bd29-72b6674ca83a", "type": "concept", "title": "Applied skins, coatings, and veneers"}, {"id": "119e1847-4fc4-4bf1-9e14-5ede2cdaee1b", "type": "concept", "title": "Texture as metaphor and material fact"}], "description": "The point is to understand how surface invites or refuses touch and how texture changes light."}, {"id": "90cad117-262e-4691-a700-028d2eeb1368", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Durability and Conservation Awareness", "children": [{"id": "731aea91-2a57-4a34-b90a-cd5574f9a36b", "type": "concept", "title": "Archival versus temporary choices"}, {"id": "138f8c97-43ae-4038-b78d-4615bf7a0146", "type": "concept", "title": "Compatibility between materials"}, {"id": "02456d5a-458d-4446-8748-ffa76b84fb7a", "type": "concept", "title": "Cleaning and repair records"}, {"id": "4c347da7-c0ea-4707-a58f-8fc89cc56347", "type": "concept", "title": "Storage, packing, and maintenance instructions"}], "description": "Students learn to anticipate aging, cracking, fading, rust, pests, water, ultraviolet exposure, and handling damage."}]}, {"id": "fc379c50-a870-4fa1-a40b-22562c6c379b", "type": "topic", "title": "Sculptural Traditions, Contemporary Sculpture, and Critical Theory", "description": "This unit situates studio work within long, contested histories. Students study sculptural traditions and contemporary theory so their work can enter larger conversations with intelligence.", "children": [{"id": "b7c85872-40bf-49a4-9b1a-2db8bf9a58e9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Historical Traditions", "children": [{"id": "df82f216-bf4e-4ca5-a534-78fb167c5f2a", "type": "concept", "title": "Ancient, classical, indigenous, African, Asian, European, and American examples"}, {"id": "e8240c11-ac53-43f5-bb86-580e4fae5ed7", "type": "concept", "title": "Ritual, memorial, religious, and civic functions"}, {"id": "56345f84-31ea-4c47-a98c-a3539eea6a73", "type": "concept", "title": "Materials and patronage"}, {"id": "2df702fd-026f-4767-8ead-d9958d6e04a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Museum display and colonial collecting histories"}], "description": "Students build a broad reference base across cultures, functions, materials, monuments, ritual objects, and museum histories."}, {"id": "fd6ac2ff-1dd6-499b-aebb-2ed73ffca635", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Modern and Contemporary Sculpture", "children": [{"id": "7d3f3a45-2dc2-457a-a7ce-995ab92c39e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Modernism and the expanded field"}, {"id": "bd54685a-b61e-4381-8128-ffa3bce42e9c", "type": "concept", "title": "Minimalism and postminimalism"}, {"id": "b6c58495-e87c-48f1-96d7-f645de0d8c45", "type": "concept", "title": "Feminist, queer, and decolonial sculpture"}, {"id": "cf92821f-d293-4eb1-9b0f-19fcba559084", "type": "concept", "title": "Ecology, technology, and global contemporary practice"}], "description": "The gist is understanding how sculpture changed through abstraction, industrial materials, minimalism, installation, performance, and new media."}, {"id": "6678ce21-b481-40ef-a737-179c965099db", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critical Theory for Makers", "children": [{"id": "2c437bd7-0bf1-4045-8ddb-fabcc868f2b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Phenomenology and embodiment"}, {"id": "1406aec8-2c03-4549-a07b-9c64e396178b", "type": "concept", "title": "Semiotics and material culture"}, {"id": "40cd555d-e211-4a2f-af1b-94dd377f7fee", "type": "concept", "title": "Institutional critique"}, {"id": "5f3a5762-808a-4a1b-856a-583464a6e969", "type": "concept", "title": "More-than-human, ecological, and networked thinking"}], "description": "Students learn useful theory as studio equipment, not as decorative vocabulary."}]}, {"id": "162997a9-9ca6-416c-b188-3fa8643ed8f0", "type": "topic", "title": "Critique, Documentation, Artist Statements, and Portfolio Development", "description": "Sculpture must be made, discussed, photographed, written about, and remembered. This unit builds habits for critique, documentation, statements, and portfolio development.", "children": [{"id": "78c6d416-1563-4b7f-b4c2-bab14fa66a31", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critique Methods", "children": [{"id": "cdac0e94-d2c1-49c3-8da2-3447c0a106f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Description before judgment"}, {"id": "6569082b-ea6c-4cf5-9a2b-6c24a54b16e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Formal, material, conceptual, and contextual critique"}, {"id": "ef81a686-1797-476f-872c-4b5b3a0f67ed", "type": "concept", "title": "Questions, evidence, and revision paths"}, {"id": "8d796f7a-1372-4e69-a9b8-87c7440c1913", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer review and self-assessment"}], "description": "Students learn to give and receive precise, generous, rigorous feedback that can change the work."}, {"id": "b41dab26-30ee-4c4e-af07-c963fd4ffb15", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Documentation", "children": [{"id": "2e2efa01-1f5e-43e8-8f9c-a99235902090", "type": "concept", "title": "Lighting and background choices"}, {"id": "2cba22e1-d6d3-4745-9a9a-8902e8c2a512", "type": "concept", "title": "Scale figures and detail shots"}, {"id": "6a1cb157-11e0-4cfb-bc5f-853d383d9742", "type": "concept", "title": "Video walkthroughs and process images"}, {"id": "c1f58e59-f60b-490b-b047-ce5f67cfeeb0", "type": "concept", "title": "File organization and metadata"}], "description": "The point is to preserve spatial work through photographs, video, diagrams, captions, and installation records."}, {"id": "f29b3502-73cd-4b84-a7ed-12b17ca1a115", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Artist Statements and Portfolio", "children": [{"id": "9c044f38-b1d4-4c55-8708-d8e414d83325", "type": "concept", "title": "Short statements and project descriptions"}, {"id": "281843a8-064e-40d1-8843-c4db64019327", "type": "concept", "title": "Material lists and dimensions"}, {"id": "0fd0aabf-d8ef-4fff-a673-e98db6e6a08f", "type": "concept", "title": "Portfolio sequencing and captions"}, {"id": "4609973f-f045-4142-bec4-bf111819e621", "type": "concept", "title": "CV, website, and application readiness"}], "description": "Students learn to make writing support the work without overexplaining it."}]}, {"id": "aefd2d20-ba05-40a5-b41d-5d35d28fa200", "type": "topic", "title": "Exhibition Design, Accessibility, Installation Safety, Rights, and Deinstallation", "description": "Exhibition planning turns finished work into a responsible public encounter. Students learn to install with attention to accessibility, hardware, labels, rights, audience safety, and deinstallation.", "children": [{"id": "9172cc3c-2193-4d3f-97ac-e8b7615e77fc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Exhibition Layout and Accessibility", "children": [{"id": "373d214e-9a96-4649-bf7a-98904f3c1a86", "type": "concept", "title": "Floor plans and object spacing"}, {"id": "7816bdc4-5137-47df-ba81-502332f1c6ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessible routes and viewing heights"}, {"id": "4e7ea90d-7152-4e93-ac2d-5c087d79967d", "type": "concept", "title": "Lighting, sound, projection, and sensory load"}, {"id": "d2fb02de-31eb-4863-849c-2768162f4f12", "type": "concept", "title": "Labels, wall text, and plain-language access"}], "description": "Students learn to design displays that respect bodies, movement, visibility, sensory access, and interpretive clarity."}, {"id": "24713b7f-8c3f-4518-b230-3f9111b46043", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Installation Safety and Rights", "children": [{"id": "c5eb7604-3fc3-433a-87e2-680a617696a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Anchoring, suspension, pedestals, barriers, and load limits"}, {"id": "d714a501-5ce7-4c9c-a1c8-cab9b953f99d", "type": "concept", "title": "Electrical, trip, sharp-edge, and fire concerns"}, {"id": "90826fb8-538a-4c51-bd80-2f73de4d6d98", "type": "concept", "title": "Image, sound, object, and participant permissions"}, {"id": "1cd2dc89-c10b-4d32-b9c9-bbba56440854", "type": "concept", "title": "Insurance, loan forms, and condition reports overview"}], "description": "The gist is to prevent harm and professionalize the practical details that make exhibitions possible."}, {"id": "4c305beb-41b5-4d9c-927c-79b3922d4e94", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Maintenance and Deinstallation", "children": [{"id": "7dfbb2a3-dec6-47cc-8c92-a78a27b7f6c9", "type": "concept", "title": "Checklists and installation manuals"}, {"id": "45fc8c6a-248d-4ea2-a695-c1d91323a70d", "type": "concept", "title": "Maintenance schedules"}, {"id": "25375fd4-863b-46ad-995b-48f029373411", "type": "concept", "title": "Packing, labeling, and storage"}, {"id": "3a3cf95f-e102-4f3d-b1ec-fc013a82173d", "type": "concept", "title": "Deinstallation, recycling, and waste planning"}], "description": "Students learn that the life of the work includes upkeep, removal, storage, disposal, and archive."}]}, {"id": "36d83f7a-50b7-4725-885c-58991a9fb127", "type": "topic", "title": "Capstone Sculpture Studio: Proposal, Prototype, Fabricate, Install, Reflect", "description": "The capstone asks students to synthesize research, design, fabrication, installation, critique, and reflection into a coherent sculptural project with professional documentation.", "children": [{"id": "0d8a6e03-d8a5-4d5a-8300-6d83990328d8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Proposal and Research", "children": [{"id": "215aa7b1-f6f9-4aea-8ba4-9fea3de0558e", "type": "concept", "title": "Concept statement and research images"}, {"id": "590c6a30-30e4-4e9e-aa1f-2d54a760d010", "type": "concept", "title": "Material tests and budget"}, {"id": "0bc49168-0659-49d0-94cb-2b86777d0786", "type": "concept", "title": "Timeline and fabrication sequence"}, {"id": "82d81de2-29fe-4d5a-a13b-9f9f84f6aa2a", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety and installation plan"}], "description": "Students learn to turn ambition into a feasible plan with references, materials, budget, timeline, and risk assessment."}, {"id": "b18918e8-7915-47db-90fb-83a0dbcc6f92", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Prototype, Fabricate, Revise", "children": [{"id": "daa85391-7c05-4aad-a2a7-d2f50390bbb8", "type": "concept", "title": "Maquettes and mockups"}, {"id": "9b753747-a77a-42dd-bf07-e95a0f6e8c3e", "type": "concept", "title": "Material tests and structural tests"}, {"id": "43bd9e9f-af96-4314-8e78-3f3a092dcd1d", "type": "concept", "title": "Critique-based revisions"}, {"id": "5b22c8bd-ecdc-45af-8c37-b3ce9015e7f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Finishing and quality control"}], "description": "The point is to make strategically: test early, fail usefully, revise visibly, and solve problems before final installation."}, {"id": "af2c5022-bb0b-450d-9916-009d6691d76d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Install, Reflect, and Archive", "children": [{"id": "c7e0f69e-2f32-4b9c-b0c0-184b3a57303d", "type": "concept", "title": "Final installation and viewer experience"}, {"id": "e2215027-f499-4d83-a90d-3acab8415990", "type": "concept", "title": "Documentation portfolio"}, {"id": "42d3c466-0bbc-40e4-b322-6ddcb052db90", "type": "concept", "title": "Artist statement and reflection"}, {"id": "2c449192-d2c1-4d67-ab94-9980561f511a", "type": "concept", "title": "Archive, storage, or deinstallation plan"}], "description": "Students complete the project by presenting it well and learning from the evidence of process."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$sculjson$::jsonb,
